course: dictionary
lesson: 1722
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses, 1) and 2). To pick the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Usually only citizens can vote for a country's government.» Here citizens means people who legally belong to a country and have its rights and duties.
explain: The second meaning is simpler: a person who lives in a town or city. To choose between the two, ask yourself: is the sentence about belonging to a country, or about living somewhere? That question usually tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Some phrases use the word in a special way. «Senior citizen» is the official term for an old person, often over 60 or 65. Fellow citizens and global citizen are other phrases you will meet in citizenship lessons.
fact: A citizen is a person who legally belongs to a country and has its rights and duties.
fact: A citizen can also be a person who lives in a town or city.
fact: «Senior citizen» is the official term for an old person, often over 60 or 65.
fact: Citizens have rights, like freedom of speech, and responsibilities, like obeying the law.
fact: Usually only citizens can vote for a country's government, but in the UK, Irish and Commonwealth citizens who live there can vote in general elections.
exercise: «Usually only citizens can vote for a country's government.» What does citizens mean here? | People who are over 65 | People who run the shops | *People who legally belong to the country | People who live in one small village
exercise: «Senior citizen» is the official term for an old person. What does senior citizen mean? | A person who lives in a town | A young person who loves sport | *An older person, often over 60 or 65 | A person in charge of a school
exercise: Citizens have rights and responsibilities. Which one is a responsibility? | *Obeying the law | Having a vote in a general election | Freedom of speech | Being able to say what you think
test: «The French Revolution spread new ideas about rights and citizens across Europe.» In this sentence, citizens means? | Animals | Shopkeepers | Old people | *People who belong to a country and have rights
test: Good citizens help their community. What does a good citizen do? | *Helps the people around them | Argues unkindly with everyone | Ignores the people around them | Lives alone and never speaks
exam: Amira says, «Only citizens can vote.» Which meaning of citizen is she using? | A person who lives in a town or city | A person who makes the laws | A person who is old | *A person who legally belongs to a country, with its rights and duties
